---
// Diagram: where human gates sit in a workflow. Harmless steps (plan, draft)
// run straight through; a risky step (send) is preceded by a gate where a
// person approves before it runs. Static SVG, token-driven colours; the gate
// is marked by shape (diamond) and the word "approve?", not colour alone.
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 460 150"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="gates-title gates-desc"
    class="diagram__svg"
  >
    <title id="gates-title">A human gate sits before each risky step</title>
    <desc id="gates-desc">
      A left-to-right workflow. The plan and draft steps run straight through.
      Before the send step - which spends, sends, or deletes - the flow stops at
      a human gate where a person approves. Only after approval does the risky
      step run.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker id="gate-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5"
        markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path class="g-arrowhead" d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    {/* flow line */}
    <line class="g-flow" x1="20" y1="60" x2="440" y2="60" marker-end="url(#gate-arrow)" />

    {/* Step 1 - plan (harmless) */}
    <rect class="g-step" x="24" y="44" width="72" height="32" rx="6" />
    <text class="g-label" x="60" y="64">plan</text>

    {/* Step 2 - draft (harmless) */}
    <rect class="g-step" x="128" y="44" width="72" height="32" rx="6" />
    <text class="g-label" x="164" y="64">draft</text>

    {/* Gate - diamond checkpoint before the risky step */}
    <path class="g-gate" d="M268 36 L300 60 L268 84 L236 60 z" />
    <text class="g-gatelabel" x="268" y="64">approve?</text>
    <text class="g-person" x="268" y="22">human</text>

    {/* Step 3 - send (risky, gated) */}
    <rect class="g-step g-step--risk" x="340" y="44" width="80" height="32" rx="6" />
    <text class="g-label" x="380" y="64">send</text>
    <text class="g-risk" x="380" y="104">sends · spends · deletes</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="diagram__cap">
    Harmless steps run free; a gate stops the flow for a person to approve
    before any step that sends, spends, or deletes.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .diagram {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
  .diagram__svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 32rem;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .diagram__cap {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .g-flow {
    stroke: var(--border);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .g-arrowhead {
    fill: var(--muted);
  }
  .g-step {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 10%, var(--surface));
    stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, var(--border));
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .g-step--risk {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 14%, var(--surface));
    stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 55%, var(--border));
  }
  .g-gate {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 16%, var(--surface));
    stroke: var(--warn);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .g-label {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .g-gatelabel {
    fill: var(--warn);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .g-person {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .g-risk {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
</style>
